{"text": "why\n\na ae Office of the General Counsel\nFisher Bulding \u00ab2011 West Grand Bd, Suite 1002 \u00ab Detrot, Mi 48202\n\nDETROIT (\u00a9 (819) 73-4528 - F (313) 672-4564\nPUBLIC SCHOOLS\n\n\u2018COMMUNITY DISTRICT detroitk12.0rg\nJuly 30, 2020\n\nVIA EMAIL only\n\u2018Chase Cantrell\n\n97 117043@reques rock.com,\nRe: _ FOIA Request No. 2021-001\nDear Mr. Cantrell:\n\nYour request to Detroit Public Schools Community District (*DPSCD\u201d) under Michigan\u2019s\nFreedom of Information Act dated Thursday, July 2, 2020, was delivered to DPSCD\u2019s FOIA\nCoordinator and per MCL \u00a715.235(1), is treated as received Monday, July 6, 2020, with an initial\nresponse due five (5) business days later, Monday, July 13 , 2020. A letter requesting a 10-business\nday extension was sent July 13, 2020.\n\nThe FOIA request seeks:\n\n1. Documents, spreadsheets, records, meeting minutes, and other materials\nrepresenting, detailing, or explaining the budget of the Detroit Public Schools\nCommunity District Police Department (the \u201cDepartment\u201d) from fiscal years\n2015-2016 through 2019-2020. As context, the budget referenced in this item\nis the one that Mr. Jeremy Vidito explained on a call with me on Wednesday,\nJune 10, 2020 at 5:05pm must be requested in writing and which information\n\u2018was supplemented by Mr. Vidito in the attached email exchange.\n\n2. Documents, spreadsheets, records, meeting minutes, and other materials\nrepresenting, detailing, or explaining expenditures related to the maintenance\nand operation of 8500 Cameron Street, Detroit, MI 48211, being the\nheadquarters of the Department.\n\n3. Anorganizational chart or any other documents, spreadsheets, records, or other\nmaterials containing information about the names, titles, or reporting\nrelationships of executive, director, or managerial level personnel for the\nDepartment.\n\n4, A list or any other documents, spreadsheets, records, or other materials\nshowing all contracts with third parties for services overseen or managed by\nthe Department, including any contracts for security personnel (e.g., Securitas)\nor support services.\n\nStudents Rise. We all Rise\n\nDPSCD does not discriminate based on race, colo, national origin, sex, disability andor religion\n\u2018Contact Compliance for more information at (313) 240-4377 or detroitk2.orgladminlcompliance.",
